  m_Name: 21 - While Loop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_while
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: While Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'A <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color></font> loop
    is used to repeat instructions as long as a condition remains true.

    Unlike
    a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>for</color></font> loop, which usually
    repeats a fixed number of times, a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color></font>
    loop continues running until the condition becomes false.


    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">energy <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#B5CEA8>3</color></font>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#6A9955># Continue moving while energy is greater than 0</color></font>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>while</color> energy <color=#D4D4D4>></color> <color=#B5CEA8>0</color>:</font>

    <indent=2em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>move_forward</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">energy <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> energy <color=#D4D4D4>-</color> <color=#B5CEA8>1</color></font></indent></indent>


    The
    loop checks the condition before each iteration.

    If the condition is true,
    the instructions inside the loop execute again.

    It is important to update
    the condition properly. Otherwise, the loop may continue forever and create an
    <color=yellow>infinite loop</color>.'
  isImageBig: 0
